  "before_interfaces": {
    "lem-galerkin-orthogonality-for-conforming-galerkin-approximations": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $V$ be a vector space over $\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, let\n$V_h\\subseteq V$ be a subspace, let $a$ be linear in its first argument and\nconjugate-linear in its second, and let $F:V\\to\\mathbb K$ be conjugate-linear.\nIf $u\\in V$ and $u_h\\in V_h$ satisfy\n$$a(u,v)=F(v)\\quad(v\\in V),\\qquad a(u_h,v_h)=F(v_h)\\quad(v_h\\in V_h),$$\nthen\n$$a(u-u_h,v_h)=0\\qquad\\text{for every }v_h\\in V_h.$$"
    ],
    "thm-adjoint-problem-for-bounded-coercive-variational-forms": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $V$ be a real or complex Hilbert space and let\n$a:V\\times V\\to\\mathbb K$ be linear in the first slot, conjugate-linear in\nthe second, bounded by $M$, and coercive with constant $\\alpha>0$:\n$$|a(u,v)|\\le M\\|u\\|_V\\|v\\|_V.$$\n$$\\operatorname{Re}a(u,u)\\ge\\alpha\\|u\\|_V^2.$$\nFor every bounded linear functional $G:V\\to\\mathbb K$, there is a unique\n$z\\in V$ such that\n$$a(v,z)=G(v)\\qquad(v\\in V),$$\nand $\\alpha\\|z\\|_V\\le\\|G\\|_{V^*}$. In the real case conjugation is the\nidentity and both forms and functionals are linear over $\\mathbb R$."
    ],
    "cor-poisson-adjoint-h2-estimate-from-global-regularity": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $n\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^n$ be a\nbounded $C^2$ domain, let $g\\in L^2(\\Omega)$, and let $z\\in H^1_0(\\Omega)$\nbe a weak solution of $-\\Delta z=g$ with zero Dirichlet data. Suppose a\nPoincaré constant $C_P$ is specified such that\n$$\\|v\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\le C_P\\|\\nabla v\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\qquad(v\\in H^1_0(\\Omega)).$$\nThen $z\\in H^2(\\Omega)$ and\n$$\\|z\\|_{H^2(\\Omega)}\\le C_{\\rm reg}(1+C_P^2)\\|g\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)},$$\nwhere $C_{\\rm reg}$ is the constant from the global H² Dirichlet regularity\ntheorem for the coefficient matrix $I$ and zero lower-order coefficients.\nThe Poincaré inequality is an explicit hypothesis here; this item does not\nimport a stronger domain or axiom branch for it."
    ],
    "lem-two-cell-hat-and-quadratic-functions-lie-in-h10": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $I=(0,1)$ and define\n$$\\phi(x)=\\begin{cases}2x,&0\\le x\\le\\frac12,\\\\2(1-x),&\\frac12\\le x\\le1,\\end{cases} \\qquad p(x)=\\frac12x(1-x).$$\nThen $\\phi|_I,p|_I\\in H^1_0(I)=W^{1,2}_0(I)$, the closure of\n$C_c^\\infty(I)$ in $W^{1,2}(I)$ ([[def-wkp-zero-as-a-sobolev-closure]])."
    ],
    "thm-cea-quasi-optimality-for-conforming-galerkin-approximations": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $V$ be a real or complex Hilbert space and let\n$a:V\\times V\\to\\mathbb K$ be linear in its first argument, conjugate-linear\nin its second, bounded by $M$, and coercive with constant $\\alpha>0$:\n$$|a(v,w)|\\le M\\|v\\|_V\\|w\\|_V,\\qquad \\operatorname{Re}a(v,v)\\ge\\alpha\\|v\\|_V^2.$$\nLet $F:V\\to\\mathbb K$ be bounded and conjugate-linear, and let $V_h\\subseteq V$\nbe finite-dimensional. Then there are unique $u\\in V$ and $u_h\\in V_h$ with\n$$a(u,v)=F(v)\\quad(v\\in V).$$\n$$a(u_h,v_h)=F(v_h)\\quad(v_h\\in V_h).$$\nThe solutions satisfy\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_V\\le\\frac M\\alpha\\inf_{v_h\\in V_h}\\|u-v_h\\|_V.$$\nThe real bilinear case uses linear functionals and reads $\\operatorname{Re}$ as\nthe identity."
    ],
    "cor-symmetric-galerkin-best-approximation-in-energy-norm": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the hypotheses and notation of\n[[thm-cea-quasi-optimality-for-conforming-galerkin-approximations]], and\nsuppose additionally that $a$ is Hermitian:\n$a(v,w)=\\overline{a(w,v)}$. Then\n$$\\|v\\|_a:=\\sqrt{a(v,v)}$$\nis the energy norm and the Galerkin solution is its best approximation:\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_a=\\inf_{v_h\\in V_h}\\|u-v_h\\|_a.$$"
    ],
    "thm-aubin-nitsche-l2-error-estimate-under-adjoint-regularity": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice and the conforming Galerkin setting of\n[[thm-cea-quasi-optimality-for-conforming-galerkin-approximations]]. Let\n$H=L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ with inner product linear in the first slot, and\nlet $J:V\\to H$ be a continuous linear inclusion with\n$\\|Jv\\|_H\\le C_E\\|v\\|_V$. Put $e:=J(u-u_h)$. The adjoint solution $z_e$ is\nthe unique element of $V$ satisfying\n$$a(v,z_e)=(Jv,e)_H\\qquad(v\\in V);$$\nit exists by [[thm-adjoint-problem-for-bounded-coercive-variational-forms]].\nLet $s\\in(0,1]$, and let $R_s\\subseteq V$ be a specified normed space of\nadjoint-regular functions. Assume constants $C_R,C_I$ independent of $h$ and\nthe error satisfy\n$$\\|z_e\\|_{R_s}\\le C_R\\|e\\|_H,\\qquad \\inf_{w_h\\in V_h}\\|z_e-w_h\\|_V\\le C_Ih^s\\|z_e\\|_{R_s}.$$\nThen\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)} \\le M C_I C_R h^s\\|u-u_h\\|_V.$$\nThe symbol $R_s$ means exactly the chosen regularity norm space in the two\ndisplayed assumptions; no fractional Sobolev interpolation estimate is\nasserted unless it verifies the second inequality. The integer endpoint may\nbe instantiated with $R_1=H^2(\\Omega)=W^{2,2}(\\Omega)$."
    ],
    "cor-shape-regular-affine-fe-primal-energy-approximation": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a\nbounded polyhedral open set with a matching shape-regular affine simplicial\nmesh family $\\{\\mathcal T_h\\}$, and set $h:=\\max_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}h_K\\le1$.\nFix an integer $r\\ge1$. On the reference simplex let\n$(\\widehat S_d,\\widehat P,\\widehat\\Sigma)$ be an unisolvent real scalar\nfinite element whose polynomial space contains $\\mathbb P_r$. Assume each\ndegree of freedom has a bounded linear extension to\n$W^{r+1,2}(\\widehat S_d)$, and let $\\widehat I$ be its interpolant. Suppose\nthere is a global map $I_h$ whose restriction to each cell is the affine\npullback of $\\widehat I$, and that $I_hu\\in V_h$ for the conforming discrete\nspace $V_h\\subset H^1_0(\\Omega)$ whenever\n$u\\in W^{r+1,2}(\\Omega)\\cap H^1_0(\\Omega)$, where $H^1_0(\\Omega)$ is the\nclosure of $C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)$ in $W^{1,2}(\\Omega)$\n([[def-wkp-zero-as-a-sobolev-closure]]). Then a constant $C$ independent of\n$h$ and $u$ satisfies\n$$\\|u-I_hu\\|_{H^1(\\Omega)}\\le C h^r|u|_{W^{r+1,2}(\\Omega)}.$$\nThe global conformity and zero-boundary mapping property of $I_h$ are explicit\nhypotheses; this estimate does not assert them for arbitrary degrees of\nfreedom."
    ],
    "cor-aubin-nitsche-h-r-plus-s-rate-under-primal-and-dual-approximation": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume Countable Choice. Assume the real scalar finite-element setting of\n[[cor-shape-regular-affine-fe-primal-energy-approximation]], and set\n$V:=H^1_0(\\Omega)$ with its usual $H^1$ norm. Let $V_h\\subseteq V$ be the\nstated conforming discrete space, let $a:V\\times V\\to\\mathbb R$ be the same\nbounded coercive form as in\n[[thm-cea-quasi-optimality-for-conforming-galerkin-approximations]], and let\n$u\\in W^{r+1,2}(\\Omega)\\cap V$ and $u_h\\in V_h$ solve the continuous and\ndiscrete equations for the same bounded linear datum $F:V\\to\\mathbb R$;\nassume also that $V_h$ is finite-dimensional. The natural inclusion\n$J:V\\to L^2(\\Omega)$ obeys $\\|Jv\\|_{L^2}\\le\\|v\\|_{H^1}$. For\n$e:=J(u-u_h)$, let $z_e$ be the adjoint solution from\n[[thm-aubin-nitsche-l2-error-estimate-under-adjoint-regularity]]. Suppose\nthere are $s\\in(0,1]$, a normed regularity space $R_s\\subseteq V$ for $z_e$,\nand constants $C_D,C_R$ independent of $h$ and $e$ such that\n$$\\|z_e\\|_{R_s}\\le C_R\\|e\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}.$$\n$$\\inf_{w_h\\in V_h}\\|z_e-w_h\\|_{H^1(\\Omega)}\\le C_D h^s\\|z_e\\|_{R_s}.$$\nThen\n$$\\|u-u_h\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\le \\frac{M^2}{\\alpha}C_{\\rm FE}C_DC_R h^{r+s}|u|_{W^{r+1,2}(\\Omega)}.$$\nHere $C_{\\rm FE}$ is the primal interpolation constant and $M,\\alpha$ are\nthe boundedness and coercivity constants of $a$. In a full-adjoint Poisson\nbranch, one may take $R_1=H^2(\\Omega)\\cap H^1_0(\\Omega)$ with the $H^2$ norm,\nprovided both displayed dual bounds hold. The $h^{r+1}$ rate is conditional\non those bounds and the primal approximation bound; no full-adjoint\nregularity is asserted on an arbitrary Lipschitz domain."
    ],
